    <h2>Approximate Nearest Neighbor (ANN) Algorithms</h2>

    <h3>How Vector DBs Scale</h3>

    <pre><code>1. HNSW (Hierarchical Navigable Small World)
   • Graph-based structure
   • Multiple layers of connections
   • Fast search: O(log n)
   • Used by: Pinecone, Weaviate, Qdrant

   [Top Layer]     A ←→ B
                   ↓     ↓
   [Mid Layer]   A ←→ C ←→ B
                 ↓   ↓   ↓
   [Bottom]    A-C-D-E-B-F-G

2. IVF (Inverted File Index)
   • Partition space into clusters
   • Search only relevant clusters
   • Trade-off: speed vs accuracy
   • Used by: FAISS, Milvus

3. Product Quantization (PQ)
   • Compress vectors for memory efficiency
   • Split vector into subvectors
   • Quantize each subvector
   • 8-10x memory reduction

4. LSH (Locality-Sensitive Hashing)
   • Hash similar vectors to same buckets
   • Probabilistic guarantees
   • Very fast, less accurate</code></pre>

